pdf.add_page(); h1("1. Project Overview & Architecture")
para("AutoSaaS AI is an autonomous user provisioning system. Takes CSV of users (email+role), validates/dedups, then uses browser automation agent to create each user in a SaaS admin console. Progress tracked in SQLite, shown live on web dashboard.")
h2("Problem Solved")
para("Manually creating 500 users in a SaaS admin console takes hours. This tool automates it with a browser agent, handles errors, supports retries, provides audit trails.")
h2("Key Features")
for f in ["CSV upload with email validation (TC1) and dedup (TC2)","Role normalization: CSV roles mapped to Admin/Manager/Member (TC3)","Idempotent retries: only re-process failed/pending (TC4)","Human-in-the-Loop approval gate","Live progress bar polling SQLite every 500ms","Audit logging for compliance","Local (Chromium) and cloud (Browserbase) browser support"]:
    bullet(f)
pdf.add_page(); h1("2. System Architecture Diagram")
diagram("FRONTEND (Browser)\n  index.html (Dashboard)  +  mock_console.html (Target SaaS Console)\n  | HTTP (fetch) |\n  v\nBACKEND (FastAPI) on port 8000\n  main.py: /api/upload-csv, /api/approve-run, /api/run-progress, /api/run-agent\n  agent.py: BrowserbaseProvisioningAgent\n  database.py: SQLite (runs, records, audit_logs)")
pdf.add_page(); h1("3. Data Flow Diagram")
diagram("USER uploads CSV\n  |\n  v\n[POST /api/upload-csv]\n  +-- Parse CSV with pandas\n  +-- Validate columns (email, role)\n  +-- TC1: Validate email regex\n  +-- Normalize: email.strip().lower(), role.strip()\n  +-- TC2: Drop duplicates by email (keep first)\n  +-- Assign IDs (REC-001, REC-002, ...)\n  +-- save_parsed_csv() -> SQLite (status='pending')\n  |\n  v\nFrontend shows Review Table (user approves)\n  |\n  v\n[POST /api/approve-run] -> status='approved'\n  |\n  v\n[POST /api/run-agent]\n  +-- Check run exists in DB\n  +-- Check non-success records exist (TC4)\n  +-- Enforce approval gate\n  +-- BrowserbaseProvisioningAgent.run()\n  |\n  v\nAgent loops over pending records:\n  +-- Normalize role (admin->Admin, etc.)\n  +-- page.evaluate(JS): open modal, fill, submit\n  +-- Read last table row -> verify email+role\n  +-- update_record_status() -> 'success' or 'failed'\n  +-- log_audit_event()\n  |\n  v\nFrontend polls GET /api/run-progress every 500ms\n  +-- completed = COUNT(status='success')\n  +-- total = runs.total_records\n  +-- percentage = completed/total * 100\n  |\n  v\nAll done -> status='completed' -> Show results table")
pdf.add_page(); h1("4. Database Schema (database.py)")
para("File: backend/database.py | 114 lines | SQLite3 + pandas")
h2("Why SQLite?")
para("Zero-config, file-based, no separate server. Perfect for single-machine provisioning. DB file persists between runs, enabling retries.")
h2("Table 1: runs")
code("CREATE TABLE runs (run_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, filename TEXT, total_records INTEGER, status TEXT)")
h2("Table 2: records")
code("CREATE TABLE records (id TEXT, run_id TEXT, email TEXT, role TEXT, status TEXT, error TEXT, PRIMARY KEY (id, run_id))")
h2("Table 3: audit_logs")
code("CREATE TABLE audit_logs (log_id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, run_id TEXT, timestamp DATETIME DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, event_type TEXT, details TEXT)")
h2("Function: init_db()")
para("Creates all 3 tables if they don't exist. Safe to call repeatedly (IF NOT EXISTS). Called on app startup and before save_parsed_csv.")
h2("Function: save_parsed_csv(run_id, filename, records)")
para("Inserts run row + all record rows. Uses INSERT OR REPLACE for idempotency. Status starts as 'pending'.")
h2("Function: get_pending_records(run_id)")
para("SELECT * FROM records WHERE run_id=? AND status != 'success'. Uses pandas read_sql_query. Returns list of dicts. This is the TC4 retry mechanism - already-successful records are skipped.")
h2("Function: update_record_status(run_id, record_id, status, error)")
para("UPDATE records SET status=?, error=? WHERE run_id=? AND id=?. Called by agent after each record. This is what drives the live progress bar.")
h2("Function: update_run_status(run_id, status)")
para("UPDATE runs SET status=? WHERE run_id=?. Tracks overall run state.")
h2("Function: log_audit_event(run_id, event_type, details)")
