pdf.add_page(); h1("9. Dependencies (requirements.txt)")
pdf.add_page(); h1("10. Test Cases TC1-TC4 Explained")
h2("TC1: Email Validation")
para("Requirement: Reject invalid email formats during CSV upload. Implementation: Regex pattern in main.py upload_csv. If any email fails, returns HTTP 400. Why: Prevents garbage data. Fail-fast.")
h2("TC2: Deduplication")
para("Requirement: Remove duplicate emails, keep first occurrence. Implementation: df.drop_duplicates(subset=['email'], keep='first'). Also normalizes emails to lowercase first. Why: Case-insensitive dedup.")
h2("TC3: Role Normalization")
para("Requirement: Map CSV roles to canonical Admin/Manager/Member, correcting the mock console's default 'Admin' bug. Implementation: role_map dict in agent.py. Default 'Member'. Agent explicitly sets dropdown value. Why: Security.")
h2("TC4: Idempotent Retries")
para("Requirement: Re-running agent only processes failed/pending records, skips successful ones. Implementation: get_pending_records() filters status != 'success'. run-agent checks retry_needed_count. Why: Saves time, avoids duplicates.")
pdf.add_page(); h1("11. Performance Optimizations")
diagram("BEFORE (slow):\n  - 4 Playwright calls per record\n  - 0.5s sleep between operations\n  - wait_for_selector before each action\n  - O(n^2) verification (scan all rows)\n  - ~2-3 seconds per record\n\nAFTER (fast):\n  - 1 page.evaluate() JS call per record\n  - No sleep, no wait_for_selector\n  - O(1) verification (read last row only)\n  - ~0.1-0.2 seconds per record\n  - ~10-20x speedup")
h2("Optimization 1: Single JS Round-Trip")
para("Playwright calls have IPC overhead (~50-100ms each). Combining 4 calls into 1 page.evaluate() eliminates 3 round-trips.")
h2("Optimization 2: Remove Sleeps")
para("Original code had time.sleep(0.5) and wait_for_selector. Since mock console is synchronous, no wait needed.")
h2("Optimization 3: Targeted Verification")
para("Original: read entire table. New: read only last row (tr:last-child). O(1) instead of O(n).")
pdf.add_page(); h1("12. Judge Q&A - Likely Questions & Answers")
qa = [("Q: How does the progress bar work?","A: Frontend polls /api/run-progress every 500ms. Backend counts records with status='success' in SQLite and returns {completed, total}. Percentage = completed/total*100."),
("Q: How do you handle errors?","A: Per-record try/except in agent.py. Failed records get status='failed' with error message. Batch continues. Failed records can be retried via TC4."),
("Q: How is security handled?","A: Role normalization (TC3) prevents privilege escalation. Email validation (TC1) prevents injection. CORS configured. Audit logs for compliance."),
("Q: Can it scale to 500+ users?","A: Yes. Optimizations make it ~10-20x faster. SQLite handles concurrent reads. Progress polling is lightweight."),
("Q: What if the agent crashes mid-run?","A: Records already processed have status='success' in DB. Re-running only processes remaining 'pending'/'failed' records (TC4). Idempotent."),
("Q: How do you test the role normalization?","A: Mock console defaults role to 'Admin' (bug). Agent explicitly sets dropdown value. Verification checks last row contains correct role."),
("Q: What is Human-in-the-Loop?","A: After CSV upload, user reviews parsed records in dashboard. Must click 'Approve & Run Agent' before automation starts."),
("Q: Why Playwright over Selenium?","A: Playwright has faster execution, better API, auto-wait, and Browserbase cloud support."),
("Q: How does Browserbase work?","A: Cloud browser service. Agent connects via CDP. Session URL provided for live viewing. Falls back to local Chromium for dev."),
("Q: What database do you use and why?","A: SQLite. Zero-config, file-based, no separate server. Persists between runs for retry support.")]
